-- title:
--   Index of ±Γ_H((qℓ)²M') in SL₂(ℤ)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes with $3 \le q$, $3 \le \ell$ and $\ell \ne q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Put $N = (q\ell)^2 M'$ and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ be `levelH (q * ℓ) M'`, the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $\Gamma_H(N) =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH N H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image, under the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(N)$, of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism sending $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ to the unit class of its lower-right entry modulo $N$; thus $\Gamma_H(N) = \{\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N) : d_\gamma \equiv 1 \bmod q\ell\}$. The assertion is the equality of natural numbers
--   $$2 \cdot \bigl[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_H(N) \vee \langle -1 \rangle\bigr] = q(q^2-1)\,\ell(\ell^2-1)\,\psi(M'),$$
--   where $\langle -1\rangle$ is the subgroup generated by $-1$, so that the join is $\pm\Gamma_H(N)$, and $\psi(M') = \sum_{d \mid M',\ d \text{ squarefree}} M'/d$ is the Dedekind psi function `dedekindPsi`. Subtraction is natural-number subtraction, harmless because $q, \ell \ge 3$.
--
--   The group $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ is the $\mathrm{diag}(q\ell,1)$-conjugate model of $\Gamma(q\ell) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, and the right-hand side is $\tfrac12\,|\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{F}_q)|\,|\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{F}_\ell)|\,\psi(M')$, the classical index of this congruence subgroup modulo $\pm 1$. It supplies the degree bookkeeping for the full-level modular curve, being used in the computation of the rank of the function field of the curve at level `levelH (q * ℓ) M'` over the field generated by the $j$-function.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_two_mul_index_gammaH_levelH_mul_sup_zpowers_neg_one_eq.lean

